{title: Wonderful Maker}
{artist: Matt Redman & Chris Tomlin}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C2]You spread out the skies over empty space
[Em7]Said, Let there be light
Into a dark and formless world Your [G/B]light was [C2]born  [D]  [Dsus]
[C2]You spread out Your ams over empty hearts
[Em7]Said, Let there be light
To a dark and hopeless world Your [G/B]Son was [C2]born  [D]  [Dsus]

{comment: Pre-Chorus}
You [Am7]made the world and [G/B]saw that it was [C2]good
You [Am7]sent Your only [G/B]son for You are [C2]good  (D/F# on the last time)

{comment: Chorus}
What a wonderful [C2]Maker, what a wonderful [Em7]Savior
How majestic Your [C2]whispers, [D/F#]how humble Your [G]love
With a strength like no [C2]other and the heart of a [Em7]Father
How majestic Your [C2]whispers, [D/F#]what a wonderful [G]God

{comment: Verse 2}
[C2]No eye has fully seen, how beautiful the cross
and [Em7]we have only heard the faintest whispers of how [G/B]great You [C2]are  [D]
